DEFINITIONS

"Software" means the MiniGuardian security suite source code — the daemon,
sentinel, terminals, consoles, and all workspace crates (miniguard,
miniguard-status, trust_core, trust_terminal, jvc_compressor, jayce_kernel,
cosmic_map, apodeixis, astraxis) — plus documentation, scripts, artifacts,
and all associated files in this repository.

"Jayce Automata Research" means Jose Almendarez and the Jayce Automata Research project.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software, in whole or in part, for
direct or indirect commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

"Weaponization" means any use of the Software, in whole or in part, to design,
develop, test, deploy, or support offensive weapons, autonomous attack systems,
surveillance infrastructure used to harm individuals, or any system intended to
cause physical, digital, or psychological harm to persons.

"Official Package" means a release package or binary of the Software exactly as
published and signed by Jayce Automata Research (for example
miniguard_<version>_amd64.deb or miniguard-<version>.x86_64.rpm), byte-for-byte
unmodified, together with its published checksums and signature.

"Dependent Program" means a program, product, operating-system image, server
image, or service of yours that installs, ships with, or requires an Official
Package in order to use MiniGuardian's protection.

"Plugin" means a program that runs inside MiniGuardian's open plugin shell and
communicates with MiniGuardian only through the Plugin Interface.

"Plugin Interface" means the published means of building Plugins: the plugin
manifest format (mg-plugin.toml), the plugin message protocol, the mg-plugin
command, the governed tools a Plugin may request, and the starter templates
created by `mg-plugin new`.

"Small Organization" means an individual, or an organization that, together with
its affiliates, had less than US$1,000,000 in gross revenue in its last fiscal
year and fewer than 25 employees and contractors.

